00:41:04.410 --> 00:41:07.260
Cutting Across the
Archive, from Photo Montage

00:41:07.260 --> 00:41:08.460
to Digital Folklore.

00:41:08.460 --> 00:41:10.200
This Advanced
Photography course is

00:41:10.200 --> 00:41:13.230
designed for students who wish
to explore photography, images,

00:41:13.230 --> 00:41:15.600
and archives as
tools and resources

00:41:15.600 --> 00:41:16.890
for artistic practices.

00:41:16.890 --> 00:41:19.380
The course focuses on the
use of archival images

00:41:19.380 --> 00:41:21.900
and photographic practices
while encouraging students

00:41:21.900 --> 00:41:26.590
to explore analog,
digital, and [AUDIO OUT]

00:41:26.590 --> 00:41:27.730
and new technologies.

00:41:27.730 --> 00:41:30.070
Through lectures,
readings, film screenings,

00:41:30.070 --> 00:41:32.620
student-driven projects,
visiting artist presentations,

00:41:32.620 --> 00:41:34.420
and critics sessions,
students experiment

00:41:34.420 --> 00:41:36.010
with a range of
artistic strategies

00:41:36.010 --> 00:41:38.190
while engaging in cross
disciplinary research

00:41:38.190 --> 00:41:40.690
and working on collaborative
and individual assignments.

00:41:40.690 --> 00:41:43.650
Across a diverse spectrum of
themes and historical context,

00:41:43.650 --> 00:41:45.880
students read and
discuss theoretical texts

00:41:45.880 --> 00:41:48.640
related to the use of archives
and artistic practices.

00:41:57.250 --> 00:42:00.160
Advance Video and Related Media.

00:42:00.160 --> 00:42:03.070
This course introduces advanced
strategies of image and sound

00:42:03.070 --> 00:42:06.190
manipulation, both
technical and conceptual.

00:42:06.190 --> 00:42:08.710
We'll cover everything from
preproduction, planning,

00:42:08.710 --> 00:42:11.260
storyboards, and scripting
through the refinement

00:42:11.260 --> 00:42:13.810
of digital editing
techniques, visual effects

00:42:13.810 --> 00:42:16.180
such as Chroma Key,
post-production,

00:42:16.180 --> 00:42:19.210
as well as audio and
sonic components.

00:42:19.210 --> 00:42:22.330
Context is provided by regular
viewings of contemporary video

00:42:22.330 --> 00:42:24.355
artworks and other
audio visual formats.

00:42:29.000 --> 00:42:31.760
Video Installation is a
contemporary and expanding art

00:42:31.760 --> 00:42:34.070
genre that intersects with
the worlds of architecture,

00:42:34.070 --> 00:42:36.770
engineering, programming,
new media, and performance

00:42:36.770 --> 00:42:37.490
practices.

00:42:37.490 --> 00:42:39.320
In this intermediate
to advanced course,

00:42:39.320 --> 00:42:41.840
students are encouraged to
expand the current themes

00:42:41.840 --> 00:42:44.330
and methods within their
art or research practices

00:42:44.330 --> 00:42:46.670
by experimenting with
various video installation

00:42:46.670 --> 00:42:50.250
strategies, such as video
mapping to 3D objects, site

00:42:50.250 --> 00:42:53.240
specific architectural projects,
multi-channel projection

00:42:53.240 --> 00:42:55.130
environments,
mixing moving image

00:42:55.130 --> 00:42:57.620
content with live performance,
wearable sculptures,

00:42:57.620 --> 00:43:01.400
live feeds, physical computing,
or other elements of interest.

